==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|pok}}, from {{inh|en|ang|poc}}, {{m|ang|pocc|t=pock; pustule; ulcer}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*pukkaz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*pukkǭ|t=pock; swelling}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*bew-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*bʰew-|t=to grow; swell}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|pok|t=pock}}, {{cog|nds|Pocke|t=pock}}, {{cog|de|Pocke|t=pock}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/pɒk/}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/pɑk/}}
*: {{rhymes|en|ɒk}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[pus]]-filled [[swelling]] on the surface on the skin [[caused]] by an [[eruptive]] [[disease]].
# Any [[pit]], especially one formed as a [[scar]]

